# Apple Native iOS & macOS SwiftUI Engineering Standards
# Targets: iOS 18+, macOS 15+, Swift 6, SwiftUI, SwiftData, StoreKit 2

## 1. Swift 6 Concurrency & Architecture
- Enable strict concurrency checking (`SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY = complete`).
- All UI state updates must happen on `@MainActor`.
- Prefer structured concurrency (`async/await`, `TaskGroup`) over legacy completion handlers or Combine where possible.
- Use Modern MVVM or Unidirectional Data Flow (State -> Action -> Reducer). Views must remain declarative and thin.

## 2. SwiftUI UI/UX Standards
- Respect Apple Human Interface Guidelines (HIG): Use dynamic type, native SF Symbols, and standard margins.
- Support Dark Mode and Light Mode automatically using semantic system colors (`Color(uiColor: .systemBackground)`).
- Provide fluid, native haptic feedback (`UIImpactFeedbackGenerator(style: .medium)`) on interactive actions.

## 3. Data Persistence & Monetization
- Use SwiftData with `@Model` for local offline storage. Never perform heavy database queries inside View bodies.
- StoreKit 2: Implement modern async transaction listener (`Transaction.updates`) and auto-entitlement verification.
- Always implement a "Restore Purchases" button visible in settings.
